fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-08T20:02:50.9457704Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-08T20:02:50.9468541Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-08T20:02:50.9469139Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-08T20:02:50.9469785Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-08T20:02:50.9470113Z 
fast	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.1	2026-10-08T20:02:50.9470375Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
